module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_non_module_fixture_fed_to_the_frontend

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { AwaitsOneGrounding, GroundingUndeclared }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, RungRead, FoundBelowTheLadder, BelowCeiling }

data a_non_module_fixture_fed_to_the_frontend: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_non_module_fixture_fed_to_the_frontend" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder,
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundBelowTheLadder,
      ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable,
      blocker: AwaitsOneGrounding { grounding: GroundingUndeclared },
      trigger_capability: "the capability to identify which corpus-collection pass admits src/v1/stage0/tests/fixtures into the whole-tree frontend subject and to bind that pass's corpus-membership predicate to the same tests/fixtures and target exclusion that run_dag_parse_sweep and compiler_tests::discover_dag_files already enforce",
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "**a 'compile the corpus' pass surfaces a PARSE FRAGMENT -- a fixture whose first token is not the 'module' keyword -- as a frontend refusal unrelated to the subject under test.** The fragment is a deliberately malformed input authored FOR the parser's own tests, so its refusal is the fixture doing its job, not a corpus defect; yet at a call site that only sees 'a file refused to parse' it is indistinguishable from a real corpus break, and can burn a hunt or block a gate on a file that was never meant to be compiled as a module.",

    "OBSERVED (producer, not transcription): during srv2 row `ef-15247-ctl-f021` (END receipt kept by calm-crab-645; artifacts under `~/runs/ef-15247-ctl-f021/out/`, chiefly `census.stderr.log`), the run `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:compile-clean-diagnostic-census --repository . --source-root dag --source-root src/v2` emitted `fact_cardinality_split_brace.dag:1:1: expected keyword 'module', found keyword 'data'`. That file lives at `src/v1/stage0/tests/fixtures/fact_cardinality_split_brace.dag`, line 1 `data split_brace_sample: ...`. The refusal was non-fatal; the instrument that produced it was retired by the 2026-10-30 process ruling, so this is an observation at the pre-deletion revision and is no longer reproducible by that route.",

    "TWO CANDIDATE PATHS ARE VERIFIED AND ARE NOT THE FEEDER. (1) `run_dag_parse_sweep` (`src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs`) is the required-CI parse phase and it EXPLICITLY SKIPS `tests/fixtures/` (the walk `continue`s on a `tests/fixtures` dir; an in-code comment records that the exclusion was once dropped, that the first consolidation run reported exactly this `fact_cardinality_split_brace.dag` failure, and that the fragment is 'on main where the parse step is GREEN' -- i.e. the exclusion is now restored). So the parse sweep does not feed it. (2) the census whole-tree subject is built by `compile_clean_whole_tree_sources_and_index` (`src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/witness_gates.rs`) over `roots = witness_layer_roots()`, and its own comment states the subject is '`dag` + `src/v2` only'; the fragment is under `src/v1`, so it is not in that subject either.",

    "UNVERIFIED HYPOTHESIS (DESIGN 4d) -- the mechanism is NOT pinned to a call site. The refusal was printed by a SHORT frontend/normalize/reconcile/analyses pass that appeared in the log BEFORE the 'compile-clean scope: whole-tree entry closure' line, which is consistent with either the src/v1 SEED's own fixture-consuming compile (the seed consumes multi-module fixtures -- see `compile_clean.rs` around `multi_module_fixture_source_digest`'s note) or the src/v1 cross-tree receipts path (`compile_clean_source_roots()` force-pushes `src/v1` into its roots, `compile_clean.rs`), neither of which is the whole-tree census subject or the parse sweep. The single feeding call site was not identified; it is asserted nowhere as fact here. To settle it: run a bounded real compile of a non-module fixture and capture which pipeline phase emits the refusal (the phase banner printed immediately before the diagnostic names it).",

    "WHATEVER THE FEEDER, the shape is the same and worth the record: a fragment authored to fail is admitted to a pass whose output is read as 'the corpus parses,' and a deliberate failure becomes noise that can be mistaken for a defect or block a refusal-on-any-error gate. The repair is to apply the SAME `tests/fixtures/` (and `target/`) exclusion the parse sweep and `compiler_tests::discover_dag_files` already apply to whichever pass is confirmed to be admitting it.",

    "DISTINCT FROM a broken subject file: here the file is a CORRECT test fragment, and the corpus is fine; only the collection predicate of the (unconfirmed) pass is too broad.",

    "SOURCES: `src/v1/stage0/tests/fixtures/fact_cardinality_split_brace.dag` line 1; `run_dag_parse_sweep` and its restored fixtures exclusion (`src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs`); `compile_clean_whole_tree_sources_and_index` 'dag + src/v2 only' (`src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/witness_gates.rs`); `compile_clean_source_roots` src/v1 force-add and the seed-fixture note (`src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/compile_clean.rs`); first observation via srv2 row `ef-15247-ctl-f021` (`census.stderr.log`).",
    "RUNG READING (this row's rung / ceiling / trigger, DESIGN 4b). FOUND BELOW THE LADDER: the harm is the silent-wrongness shape -- a fragment authored to fail is admitted to a pass whose output is read as 'the corpus parses', so a deliberate failure becomes false noise that can be mistaken for a defect or block a refusal-on-any-error gate -- which DESIGN 4b places below the ladder. The rung is stated WITHOUT a rung number because the FEEDER MECHANISM STAYS UNGROUNDED: which pass admits the fixture is not identified (the two candidate paths are verified NON-feeders; the frontend/refusal source remains an unconfirmed hypothesis, DESIGN 4d), so no GuaranteeRung is asserted. CEILING = mechanically preventable, and the reason it sits THERE and not lower: once the feeder is identified, admitting the fixture is a DECIDABLE membership error -- the SAME `tests/fixtures/` and `target/` exclusion the parse sweep already enforces supplies the predicate, and a discriminating fixture plus a positive module routed through the real feeder would mechanically block the mis-admission. A missing grounding belongs in the BLOCKER, it does NOT lower the ceiling; and this row claims NO structurally-guaranteed/impossible rung -- the prevention is mechanical (a decidable exclusion the instrument applies), not a structural impossibility. BLOCKER = awaits one grounding, grounding authority not yet declared: the climb to that mitigation waits on identifying the admitting pass (GroundingUndeclared). TRIGGER = a capability, NOT 'rerun the instrument': the capability to identify the real feeder's corpus-membership rule and bind it to the existing exclusion predicate (the WHATEVER-THE-FEEDER receipt above states the repair this capability must land).",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
